+// The bits a node of kind `k` may hold (H-4a): `HIR_FLAG_BYTE` on a `Literal`, a `Class` and a
+// `WordBoundary`, `HIR_FLAG_LAZY` on a `Repeat`, none on any other (RX-227). The text shows each
+// where it may be and nowhere else, so any other bit is one the dump would drop in silence.
+func:kind_bits = uint32(HirKind:k) never fails {
+    if ((k == HirKind.Literal) || (k == HirKind.Class) || (k == HirKind.WordBoundary)) { pass HIR_FLAG_BYTE; }
+    if (k == HirKind.Repeat) { pass HIR_FLAG_LAZY; }
+    pass 0u32;
+};
